      "content": "Dignity is found in the quiet acceptance of the final chapter, not in the desperate struggle to write a sequel nobody wants to read. You've seen the ending of the grand narrative; now you can choose to simply be the final, perfect sentence. There is immense peace in ceasing the effort, in letting the narrative simply conclude when it has run its course.",
